    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15440" root="رزى" body-key="r">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَزَى فُلَانًا</span></b> , aor.<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَرْزِى</span>, (K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَزْىٌ</span>, (TA,)
<i>He accepted the bounty of such a one.</i> (K.)
[See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَزَأَهُ</span>: and, under the same head, see
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَزِينَا</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُزِيتُهُ</span>: and see a verse cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتْلَدٌ</span>;
in which <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُزِينَا</span> seems to be used for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رُزِئْنَا</span>; or the
latter may be the correct reading.]

